      <activity id="22e4c1e6-e194-56df-8ca5-d6983cb1e44e" activityNameId="67d8bd6d-cb88-542a-93d2-ff0124e155c8" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="2" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Disposal, building, window frame, wood-metal, opaquely painted, Baumgartner, wall opening, to final disposal</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Disposal, building, window frame, wood-metal, opaquely painted, Baumgartner, wall opening, to final disposal
The amount of materials to be disposed of at the end of life was estimated based on the bill of materials. A cut-off approach is used for recycling of metals. The functional unit is 1m2 of wall opening.;
UUID: e07cc654-6748-44cc-95bd-6c197a919a64
Included processes are the disposal of production materials. The transport to the municipal incineration plant is included.
Location: Data apply to the supply in Switzerland.
Technology: Saphir integral 55/55; Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at window manufacturer Baumgartner in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_e07cc654-6748-44cc-95bd-6c197a919a64.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
